.TH BACKGAMMON 6.SH NAMEbackgammon \- the game of backgammon.SH SYNOPSIS\fBbackgammon\fR[\-n] [\-r|\-w|\-b] [\-p[rwb]] [\-s file] [file].SH DESCRIPTIONBackgammon against the computer, on a board of numbered points drawn incharacters.  It asks at the start whether you want instructions.  A moveis typed as the starting point and the finishing point,\fB8-5\fR,\fRor the starting point and the roll,\fB8/3\fR;\fReach die is moved separately..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-n\fRdo not ask about instructions..TP 12\fB\-r\fRyou play red..TP 12\fB\-w\fRyou play white..TP 12\fB\-b\fRyou play both sides..TP 12\fB\-p\fIx\fRprint the board before each move of red\fR(\fBr\fR),\fRwhite\fR(\fBw\fR)\fRor both\fR(\fBb\fR).\fR.TP 12\fB\-s\fI file\fRcarry on the game saved in\fIfile\fR.\fRA file named without\fB\-s\fRdoes the same..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOteachgammon, back